# Wishes (wishes.ron) and reactions to a served item (design/handson.md §3.4–3.5).
# English placeholder texts in every language until T9 (see handson_TODO.txt).

# --- generic wishes ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
wish.long_day
* Something warm, not too sweet — long day.

wish.wake_me
* Something strong. I've still got four hours of driving.

wish.hands_cold
* Anything warm to hold. My hands are frozen.

wish.train_soon
* Whatever's fastest — my train's in ten minutes.

wish.earned_it
* Something sweet. I've earned it.

wish.surprise_me
* Surprise me. Something I'd never order.

wish.skipped_dinner
* Something filling. I skipped dinner. And lunch.

wish.sleepy_not_awake
* Something gentle. I'm trying to get sleepy, not awake.

wish.club_oven
* Something cold — the club was an oven.

wish.taste_of_home
* Something that tastes like home. Anyone's home.

wish.exam_at_eight
* Fuel. I've got an exam at eight.

wish.soaked
* Something with spice — I'm soaked to the bone.

wish.not_coffee
* Anything but coffee. I've had six.

wish.for_my_friend
* Something pretty — it's my friend's birthday.

wish.goes_with_snow
* Something that goes with snow.

wish.on_the_side
* Just a little something on the side.

wish.bitter_mood
* Bitter. Like my mood. No sugar.

wish.headache
* Something fresh, please. I've got a headache.

wish.slow_sip
* Something to sip slowly while the rain does its thing.

wish.engaged
* We just got engaged! Something special!

wish.one_hand
* Something I can drink with one hand — I'm flying a drone with the other.

wish.patrol
* Strong, to go. Quiet night so far — let's keep it that way.

wish.like_grandma_made
* Something like my grandmother made? She was from Lviv.

wish.childhood
* Something from when I was a kid.

wish.three_am
* It's three in the morning. I don't know what I want.

wish.kind_coffee
* Wake me up gently — coffee, but kind.

wish.fog_outside
* Something warm. You can't see the station through this fog.

# --- personal wishes --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
wish.mirek.like_lida
* Black, Karolina. The way Lida poured it.

wish.mirek.tired_eyes
* Something for tired eyes, eh? Not that mine are tired.

wish.mirek.walked
* I walked here tonight. Something to warm an old man.

wish.hana.twelve_minutes
* I've got twelve minutes. Something hot and fast.

wish.hana.blanket
* Shift's over, Karolina. Something that feels like a blanket.

wish.vera.properly
* Tea. Properly made, mind you — no bag-dunking.

wish.vera.lidas_kolac
* Your grandmother's koláč was better, Karolina. Show me yours.

wish.vera.she_would_make
* Make me something Lida would have made.

wish.filip.cheapest
* The cheapest coffee that still counts as coffee?

wish.filip.passed
* I passed! Something fancy — my treat.

wish.radek.to_go
* To go. The 01:12 won't dispatch itself.

wish.radek.last_shift
* Last shift, Karolina. Make it a good one.

wish.radek.no_rush
* No rush tonight. Something slow.

wish.lori.one_song
* One hot chocolate, paid in one song?

wish.lori.my_voice
* Something for my voice. Honey, maybe?

wish.guest_333.two_sugars
* Tea. With lemon. Two sugars.

wish.guest_anwar.oat
* An oat flat white, please. And maybe the Wi-Fi password.

# --- generic reactions ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
react.perfect.1
* Oh. That's exactly it.

react.perfect.2
* How did you know?

react.perfect.3
* I'm coming back tomorrow just for this.

react.perfect.4
* That's the one. Thank you.

react.perfect.5
* You read my mind. Or my face.

react.good.1
* Mm. Lovely.

react.good.2
* That hits the spot.

react.good.3
* Thank you, really.

react.good.4
* Oh, that's nice. Warm all the way down.

react.good.5
* Just what the night needed.

react.okay.1
* Nice, thanks.

react.okay.2
* Not what I pictured, but nice.

react.okay.3
* Warm. Good.

react.okay.4
* That'll do me fine.

react.okay.5
* Thanks — it's good.

react.not_quite.1
* Not quite it — but thank you for trying.

react.not_quite.2
* Hm. Different. I like that you tried.

react.not_quite.3
* Not what I meant, but it's warm. That counts.

react.not_quite.4
* Funny — I'd never have picked this. Thanks.

react.not_quite.5
* It's fine, honestly. You've got your hands full.

# --- regulars' reactions ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
react.mirek.perfect
* …Almost like hers, Karolina. Almost.

react.mirek.good
* Good. Strong enough to keep a taxi awake.

react.mirek.okay
* It's coffee. I've had worse. From robots.

react.mirek.not_quite
* Hm. Lida would've laughed. Drinkable, though.

react.hana.perfect
* Oh, that's exactly it. You saved my night.

react.hana.good
* Hot and quick. You're a hero.

react.hana.okay
* Thanks — that'll get me to the next round.

react.hana.not_quite
* Not quite, but it's warm. That's what counts at three.

react.guest_333.perfect
* …

react.guest_333.good
* …

react.guest_333.okay
* …

react.guest_333.not_quite
* …

react.vera.perfect
* Well. Lida would have grumbled, but she'd have drunk it.

react.vera.good
* Properly done. I'll allow it.

react.vera.okay
* Acceptable. Your grandmother had steadier hands.

react.vera.not_quite
* Hm. We'll keep practising, you and I.

react.filip.perfect
* Okay, this is unreal. I'm writing my thesis about it.

react.filip.good
* That's good. Like, actually good.

react.filip.okay
* Thanks! Caffeine is caffeine.

react.filip.not_quite
* Interesting… I'll drink it anyway, I'm a student.

react.radek.perfect
* Ha. Right on time, and just right.

react.radek.good
* Good one. The trains will run better for it.

react.radek.okay
* Does the job. Like a timetable.

react.radek.not_quite
* Not my usual, but I won't report you.

react.lori.perfect
* Oh, I could sing about this one.

react.lori.good
* Mm. My voice thanks you.

react.lori.okay
* That's sweet of you. Thank you.

react.lori.not_quite
* Not quite my key — but lovely of you to try.
